    "title": "Real Madrid 1-1 Girona: La Liga – as it happened",
    "text": "10 Apr 2026 - 21:37 (21:37 GMT)That’s a wrap!That’s it for our live coverage of Real Madrid 1-1 Girona from the Santiago Bernabeu.Click here to read the match report of what was an eventful game in the Spanish capital, and don’t forget to stick with us for all the top sporting events over the course of the weekend, including Tyson Fury v Arslanbek Makhmudov and the huge Premier League clash between Chelsea and Manchester City!Thanks for keeping us company.10 Apr 2026 - 21:30 (21:30 GMT)A worrying trend for Real Madrid?Real Madrid head to Munich in midweek needing to win the game to have any chance of going through to the UEFA Champions League semifinals.They may well have to change the below trend if that’s to happen … 0 – Real Madrid have failed to score in the first half of each of their last four matches in all competitions, their worst run without a first-half goal since September 2024 (six). Stuck. pic.twitter.com/68QW73MhSr — OptaJose (@OptaJose) April 10, 202610 Apr 2026 - 21:25 (21:25 GMT)A big weekend of sport on Al Jazeera!Aside from La Liga football, there’s plenty more sport coming your way on Al Jazeera this weekend.On Saturday, we bring you some blockbuster boxing action as former world heavyweight champion Tyson Fury makes his comeback against Russian-born heavyweight Arslanbek Makhmudov at the Tottenham Hotspur Stadium.Then on Sunday, we bring you live coverage of the mouthwatering Premier League clash between Chelsea and Manchester City at Stamford Bridge.10 Apr 2026 - 21:24 (21:24 GMT)Read all about it: Real held at home as Barca eye titleOur match report following the game in Madrid is now live.10 Apr 2026 - 21:20 (21:20 GMT)A frustrating night for Kylian MbappeKylian Mbappe had his chances against Girona, but the French superstar was found wanting when his side needed him most.The Frenchman got into some great areas but either took too many touches or snatched at his efforts and cut a frustrated figure at full-time as the teams trudged off.Vinicius Jr also put in a below-par display, and Real Madrid will need both of them to be back to their best against Bayern Munich on Wednesday night.10 Apr 2026 - 21:12 (21:12 GMT)All eyes on MunichNext up for Real Madrid is the crucial second leg of their UEFA Champions League quarterfinal with Bayern Munich on Wednesday.Los Blancos head to Bavaria, trailing 2-1 from the first leg. And with the league title now Barcelona’s to lose, Real Madrid’s season rests on beating Bayern in their own backyard.Can they do it? Of course they can, it’s Real Madrid. But tonight’s display hardly left their fans brimming with confidence.Full Time: Real Madrid 1-1 Girona10 Apr 2026 - 21:09 (21:09 GMT)A very valuable point for GironaFew were expecting Girona to come away from the Spanish capital with anything other than a loss tonight, but Michel’s side thoroughly deserved their point.After riding out what was a rough opening 10 minutes, Michel’s side changed their tactical shape and caused Real Madrid plenty of headaches.The draw keeps them in 12th place, and takes them to 38 points for the season – nine clear of the relegation zone.Full Time: Real Madrid 1-1 Girona10 Apr 2026 - 21:03 (21:03 GMT)A season-defining result for Real Madrid?It’s a frustrating evening at the Bernabeu for Real Madrid, and it could well be the result that seals another La Liga title for rivals Barcelona.Despite taking a 51st-minute lead through Fede Valverde, Girona grabbed a deserved equaliser through Thomas Lemar 10 minutes later, and the hosts just couldn’t find a late winner.The draw leaves Real Madrid six points behind leaders Barcelona, who face Espanyol later this round.Full Time: Real Madrid 1-1 GironaGet instant alerts and updates based on your interests. Be the first to know when big stories happen.10 Apr 2026 - 20:59 (20:59 GMT)Full time! It ends all squareThe referee sounds his whistle slightly before the six minutes of additional time are completed here at the Santiago Bernabeu, and the whistles and jeers ring out around the stadium.The home crowd aren’t happy with the point, but Girona are worthy of the draw. Real Madrid just couldn’t find the attacking spark needed to take all three points.Full Time: Real Madrid 1-1 Girona10 Apr 2026 - 20:55 (20:55 GMT)Time is running outGirona are doing their best to eat up the clock here as Rincon goes down after a tussle with Vinicius Jr.Real Madrid win the free-kick, but again, it amounts to nothing.90+4 mins: Real Madrid 1-1 Girona",
